{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UFUaYTwzQiL3ZqrYGjsGBV","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Concrete implementations of [`crate::tls`] / [`crate::crypto`]\n2\t//! traits, one submodule per backend.\n3\t//!\n4\t//! The application picks one of these at QUIC-context construction\n5\t//! time and hands it the [`crate::tls::TlsBackend`] surface; the\n6\t//! rest of picoquic stays generic over the chosen backend.\n7\t//!\n8\t//! Submodules are gated by Cargo features so a binary only pays\n9\t//! for the backends it actually uses.\n10\t//!\n11\t//! This module only declares backend submodules; concrete backend\n12\t//! implementations live behind their feature gates.\n13\t\n14\t#[cfg(feature = \"sys-picotls\")]\n15\tpub mod picotls;\n16\t\n17\t#[cfg(feature = \"sys-openssl\")]\n18\tpub mod openssl;\n19\t\n20\t/// Load or unload the mbedtls crypto provider.  In the C implementation\n21\t/// this populates the global cipher-suite / key-exchange registry when\n22\t/// `PICOQUIC_WITH_MBEDTLS` is defined; without that flag the C body is\n23\t/// an explicit no-op (`/* Nothing to do, as the module is not loaded. */`).\n24\t/// Rust selects backends directly rather than through a global registry,\n25\t/// so this is a no-op until a `sys-mbedtls` feature and submodule are\n26\t/// added.\n27\t/// C: `picoquic_mbedtls_load`.\n28\tpub fn mbedtls_load(_unload: bool) {}\n29\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e2dc405c-b85c-47a3-92e4-53e1c53f419b","uuid":"2fde4116-2bf1-487f-84f0-be89166083b1","timestamp":"2026-05-07T08:12:00.357Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/sys/mod.rs","content":"//! Concrete implementations of [`crate::tls`] / [`crate::crypto`]\n//! traits, one submodule per backend.\n//!\n//! The application picks one of these at QUIC-context construction\n//! time and hands it the [`crate::tls::TlsBackend`] surface; the\n//! rest of picoquic stays generic over the chosen backend.\n//!\n//! Submodules are gated by Cargo features so a binary only pays\n//! for the backends it actually uses.\n//!\n//! This module only declares backend submodules; concrete backend\n//! implementations live behind their feature gates.\n\n#[cfg(feature = \"sys-picotls\")]\npub mod picotls;\n\n#[cfg(feature = \"sys-openssl\")]\npub mod openssl;\n\n/// Load or unload the mbedtls crypto provider.  In the C implementation\n/// this populates the global cipher-suite / key-exchange registry when\n/// `PICOQUIC_WITH_MBEDTLS` is defined; without that flag the C body is\n/// an explicit no-op (`/* Nothing to do, as the module is not loaded. */`).\n/// Rust selects backends directly rather than through a global registry,\n/// so this is a no-op until a `sys-mbedtls` feature and submodule are\n/// added.\n/// C: `picoquic_mbedtls_load`.\npub fn mbedtls_load(_unload: bool) {}\n","numLines":29,"startLine":1,"totalLines":29}}}
